Retro68 LaunchAPPL: start Mini vMac's executable directly (MacMusic, 2026-10-01)

Apply to Retro68 commit f3b44a4 (2026-09-26), then rebuild Retro68:
    cd ~/Retro68 && git apply ~/MacPlusProjects/MacMusicPlayer/tools/patches/retro68-launchappl.patch

What it does: when minivmac-path names an app bundle, LaunchAPPL ran
"open -nWa <bundle>"; with this change it runs the bundle's executable
(Contents/MacOS/minivmac) itself, as its child process.

Why: the change was made on 2026-10-01 while setting up the toolchain,
before the project's recorded sessions, and its reason wasn't written
down. What is known: with it, LaunchAPPL waits for Mini vMac and stops it
at --timeout (shown by the 1.0 smoke-test hang check), which
tests/run-smoke.sh and tools/make-release.sh rely on. LaunchAPPL hasn't
been tried without it since. An earlier LaunchAPPL build from the same
day, probably from before the change, is kept as
~/Retro68-build/toolchain/bin/LaunchAPPL.old.

diff --git a/LaunchAPPL/Client/MiniVMac.cc b/LaunchAPPL/Client/MiniVMac.cc
index 5750110c2d..6ed4001baf 100644
--- a/LaunchAPPL/Client/MiniVMac.cc
+++ b/LaunchAPPL/Client/MiniVMac.cc
@@ -556,7 +556,11 @@ bool MiniVMacLauncher::Go(int timeout)
     fs::current_path(tempDir);
 #ifdef __APPLE__
     if(vmacIsAppBundle)
-        return ChildProcess("open", {"-nWa", vmacPath.string()}, timeout) == 0;
+    {
+        fs::path executable =
+            vmacPath / "Contents" / "MacOS" / "minivmac";
+        return ChildProcess(executable.string(), {}, timeout) == 0;
+    }
 #endif
     return ChildProcess(vmacPath.string(), {}, timeout) == 0;
 }
